<!--
  STATE.md.tmpl — run-state file template (PLAN.md §5 "Memory & resume").

  WHERE THIS FILE LIVES ON DISK (not in git):
    $CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA/runs/<slug>/STATE.md

  This is ephemeral, per-machine plugin data — it is NOT committed to the
  worktree branch and is NOT git-tracked at all. It exists purely so a
  brand-new session with zero context can resume a run (usage-limit /
  crash survival). The run's actual deliverable — `plan.md` — is the
  artifact that DOES get committed to the worktree branch; see
  `templates/plan.md.tmpl` and `templates/README.md` for that half of the
  split.

  FILL-IN CONVENTION: replace every `<angle-bracket>` placeholder below.
  Checkbox sections use `- [ ]` / `- [x]` per item, matching PLAN.md §5's
  own example verbatim.

  FRONTMATTER NOTE: `last_seen` is NOT part of the initial file — it is
  injected by `hooks/state-checkpoint.sh` (Stop + SubagentStop hook) the
  first time the run stops, and re-stamped on every stop after that. Do
  not author it here; the hook adds it as the first frontmatter key. The
  hook also owns re-stamping `phase` when `$LITE_PHASE` is set — keep this
  file's `phase:` key name and its enum exactly as below so the hook's
  `frontmatter_has "phase"` / overwrite logic matches on the first try.
-->
